{"author":{"id":"8022379585b4ab99ca8775db3eb67d33fcb256817114c28e51ccc1e9f55cdec4"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1792310743,"nonce":"cBlPwd7QFA39ziuym7XL89UyZPc=","title":"2026-09-20 e762f2e7/c39d1cf4/9e76c2d5 (581-\u003e591) — haxe.ds.Vector fixed the RIGHT way (typedef-\u003eextern Vec, abstract ctors as methods, ...","message":"User asked for \"the right fix\" for haxe.ds.Vector (abstract over\n`rayzor.Vec\u003cT\u003e` through `private typedef VectorData\u003cT\u003e`), not an alias.\n\n**Root causes, in order found:**\n1. rayzor DEFINES `eval` (masquerade, compilation/mod.rs). Vector.hx's\n   `#elseif eval` branches came BEFORE our `#elseif rayzor` ones, so the\n   typedef was `eval.Vector\u003cT\u003e`, which resolved by bare name to... `Vector`\n   itself. Any stdlib file with an eval branch ahead of a rayzor branch is\n   suspect. Fixed by reordering (tolerated per-target edit) and\n   `(eval \u0026\u0026 !rayzor)` on eval-only branches.\n2. `rayzor.Vec` was ITSELF broken: externs.rs auto-registered the\n   `@:generic extern class`'s bodyless methods as bare symbols\n   (`class_key(\"rayzor.Vec\")` resolved) shadowing the VecI32/VecF64/VecPtr\n   monomorph rows → alloc+ctor, \"can't resolve symbol push\". Skip GENERIC\n   externs that have monomorph variants.\n3. Abstract constructors with bodies NEVER ran: tast_to_hir inlined only a\n   single `this = e`; anything else value-wrapped the first arg (`new A(3)`\n   → `this = 3`). Now lowered as a method with `this` = receiver slot +\n   appended `return this`; `new` calls it with a zero underlying;\n   `extern overload` ctors get `new_\u003carity\u003e` symbols. Bodyless\n   (`@:multiType`) keep the wrap.\n4. `@:op([])` (not just `@:arrayAccess`) marks array access; imported\n   abstracts resolve it via `SymbolFlags::ARRAY_ACCESS` by arity; when the\n   inline fails a real method call is emitted. `[]` on a `rayzor.Vec` maps\n   to VecX_get/set in MIR (`vec_index_class`).\n5. Typedef-as-Class alias rule extended to EXTERN class targets (Vec shows\n   as `Abstract` kind pre-lowering — accept Class|Abstract with EXTERN flag).\n6. `this.m()` inside an abstract: underlying's methods FIRST, then the\n   abstract's own (Map still works: IMap has set/get...; only Map.copy was\n   already broken).\n7. `new Vector\u003cFloat\u003e(n)` dropped its type args (declared params kept) →\n   erased `get` returns not bitcast. Also: erased-return machinery ignored\n   Abstract receivers (3 sites), FUNCTION_MAP path typed an import's erased\n   return as the caller's Float (fptosi instead of bitcast) → `IrType::I64`\n   when `callee_returns_type_param`; f64 into an erased i64 slot bitcasts;\n   Int index into i64 wrapper slot must widen (garbage upper bits looked like\n   \"5-5-5\" = element 0 read every time — only under certain register state).\n8. `dynamic_box_at` dereferenced any aligned address ≥0x1000: raw f64 bits\n   (0x4004...) segfaulted the erased-return unboxer. Reject `addr\u003e\u003e47 != 0`.\n9. **`Null\u003cBool\u003e` truthiness**: since `?q:Bool` is Null\u003cBool\u003e, `if (q)`,\n   `!q`, `\u0026\u0026`/`||`, guards compared the BOX POINTER; `f(false)` took the\n   true branch; TestXML's attribute quoting flipped between builds by\n   pointer parity. `truth_of()` at every truth site.\n10. `try_array_runtime_call` hijacked ANY `x.join(sep)` regardless of\n    receiver (Vector.join printed the Vec capacity slot).\n11. `try_inline_abstract_method`'s BY-NAME fallback matched an unrelated\n    abstract's static `test` for `inst.test()` and inlined it — dropping the\n    call (Issue6175 lost). Only surfaced once expression-form\n    `function f() return x;` bodies became inlinable. Now by-name only for\n    the receiver's own abstract, or a decayed (non-named) receiver type.\n\n**Still open:** Vector\u003cString\u003e.join / Std.string(T) inside generic code\n(erasure: raw pointer, no runtime type); in-file generic abstracts with\nT-typed locals → `[trap-stub:generic]`; Issue6752 ctor-as-value\n(`CsStack.new`) now CRASH (was WRONG); Issue9123 @:forward abstract op.\n\n**Method:** probes in scratchpad/probe (V*/W*/X*/F*/J*/K*/AA*/NB.hx). A\n`for` over variants rewriting ONE file gave identical output — the\ncompilation result is cached by path+mtime within a second; use distinct\nfile names. `RAYZOR_LOWER_TRACE` prints per-probe \"lowered by\"; an\nuntraced direct call = the FUNCTION_MAP path in call/mod.rs.\n\nRelated: [[bugs_array_clamp_regressed_nbody_and_method_values]],\n[[bugs_rest_args_and_abstract_type_params]],\n[[bugs_optional_int_params_and_null_scalar_operands]].\n\n- Index summary moved from MEMORY.md (2026-10-18): 2026-09-20 e762f2e7+c39d1cf4+9e76c2d5 (581-\u003e591): haxe.ds.Vector fixed properly — the `eval` DEFINE put eval branches ahead of rayzor ones; rayzor.Vec itself was dead (bare-symbol auto-registration); ABSTRACT CTORS WITH BODIES NEVER RAN; `@:op([])`; Null\u003cBool\u003e TRUTHINESS read the box pointer; any `.join()` was Array.join; by-name abstract inlining trap.\n\n---\nArchived from Claude memory `bugs_vector_over_vec_abstract_ctors_null_bool` on 2026-10-18. A record of past work; open items in it may have their own issues.","files":null}]}